# Line endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set on the Windows workstation this project is edited from,
# and it rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout everywhere. That is invisible for TypeScript
# and harmless for it, but a shell script with CRLF does not run on the server: bash
# reads the carriage return as part of the command and fails with
# `deploy.sh: line 12: $'\r': command not found` — at runtime, on the deploy path, not
# at review time.
#
# So the two things that must stay LF are pinned here rather than left to whoever
# happens to have autocrlf off.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf

# Generated artefacts and local databases, kept out of diffs and out of line-ending
# negotiation: a conflict inside either is noise.
prisma/generated/** text eol=lf
*.db binary
*.db-wal binary
*.db-shm binary
*.db-journal binary

# Prisma's own client output. The project already ignores this path in .gitignore,
# where the Prisma-generated comment explains why; repeating it here would only
# create a second place to keep in step.